# SHA256SUMS in this folder

`SHA256SUMS` is the checksum list from the complete frozen snapshot
`/workspace/octavo_n3_004` (376 files). Paths are relative to that snapshot
root (for example `./rust/src/lib.rs`).

This repository copy omits `lab/`, `results/`, and `attack_retest/` (lab
search trees, bench logs, and the attack-crate copy), plus a few historical
lab notes (`PROGRESS.md`, `PROGRESS_003.md`, `REPORT_003_fallback1.md`,
`REPORT_bfast1_from_002.md`, `SHA256SUMS_fallback1.txt`, `SNAPSHOT_NOTE.md`,
`SNAPSHOT_from_002.md`). Those lines in `SHA256SUMS` have no matching file
here.

`README.md` in this folder is the experimental repo README, not the freeze
README, so its hash will not match `SHA256SUMS`. `MIGRATION.md`,
`migrate.py`, and this note are new and are not in the freeze list. Every
other file that is present should still match its listed hash:

```
cd n3 && grep '  \./rust/src/lib.rs$' SHA256SUMS | sha256sum -c
```

The omitted paths were left out of git on purpose; they are not a
corruption of the freeze. The full snapshot remains on the lab machine.

Octavo is still homemade; for real secrets use AES-GCM-SIV, age, or libsodium.
